n: 3.8.2
name: miniature
kind: hub
is: mini-nums is 687 lines of Python that intern blueprint and recipe trees under four-integer ids in arrival order. Nothing evaluates a recipe or holds a value. All 7 tests (15 assertions) pass; one compares a constant with itself and two assert only counts. Probes show names outside identity, field order inside, and rebinding that moves only a name.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.2.3
name: mini-cell-records
kind: observation
is: A mini-nums Blueprint is (module, id, name), a Recipe is (module, category, blueprint, children) and a NamedCell is (module, name, base, blueprint, access recipe, constructor id). A global's constructor is the interned Block(access, Write(=, access, init)). An object's field cells are built and dropped: after three objects cells_by_name is empty.
status: observed
src: 2.16.5#221-226 2.16.5#248-259 2.16.5#276-284 2.16.5#293-317 2.16.5#331-335
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.2.4
name: no-evaluator
kind: observation
is: No function in mini-nums evaluates anything: of 49 callables the only name matching eval, run, value or call is RID_call, an id constructor, and neither Recipe nor NamedCell has a value field. 'let x = 2 + 3 * 4' yields a cell with constructor 1.6.3.1 and the literal table {2:1, 3:2, 4:3}; 14 is computed nowhere, and 'let z = 1 / 0' is accepted.
status: observed
src: 2.16.5#248-284 2.16.6#110-120 2.16.28 2.16.8#45-55
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.2.6
name: test-4-is-a-tautology
kind: observation
is: Test 4 of mini-nums, named cross-language structural equivalence, compares cells[0].blueprint, which calc.py line 114 sets to the constant BID_integer() for every literal, with BID_integer() called directly; the schema's blueprint is unused. With the schema field changed to a string, both compared ids are still 1.1.2.2.
status: observed
src: 2.16.7#93-102 2.16.6#114 2.16.8#35-43
why: In the changed probe the schema's actual blueprint is 1.3.1.1, holding 1.2.1.2+1.1.2.4 (an object of one string), and plays no part in the comparison.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.3
name: phase-mapping
kind: hub
is: The mapping blueprint = ice, recipe = water, cell = gas is first written on 2026-05-08, in the folder's READMEs and docstrings. NUMS.Go has none of the words. Earlier (2025-09, 2026-03) ice, water and gas named a persistence state of a node. The body declared state orthogonal to kind on 2026-06-08; one old-body grammar file keeps the old mapping.
at: 2026-11-24

