n: 3.8.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Seven things to carry: the cell as a four-part declared slot; rebinding that moves only a name; a conscious choice on field names and order in identity; tests where each side derives the id; state as an axis independent of kind; the 2025-09 persistence meaning of ice, water and gas as candidate definition; a run-time cell as blueprint plus value.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.8.1
name: cell-as-four-part-slot
kind: finding
is: Carry forward the cell as a four-part declared slot: an access recipe, a base blueprint, a name and a constructor recipe, with the constructor stored as a recipe and referred to by id. NUMS.Go's own NamedCell_t record has that form, and mini-nums reproduces the form and checks it in its test 3.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.8.4.5 3.8.2.3
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.8.8.7
name: runtime-cell-as-blueprint-plus-value
kind: finding
is: Take NUMS.Go's unused Cell_t {*Blueprint_t; Value any} from NUMS.Go as the starting form of a run-time cell: a blueprint plus a value. Neither the folder nums-go-2023 nor mini-nums mentions that record, and nothing else in NUMS.Go lets a cell hold a value.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.8.4.5
at: 2026-11-24

